<urn:atm:triage:finding/AXPE-RSH-003>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AXPE-RSH-003" ;
  triage:title "Herdr wake-up rejection warn! lacks subsystem/action fields" ;
  triage:description "The tracing::warn! in HerdrReceivedHook::emit_received_message at crates/atm-daemon-bootstrap/src/received_hook_selector.rs:445 (\"Herdr wake-up was not accepted\") omits the subsystem= and action= fields carried by the sibling warn!/error! sites in the same module and in crates/atm-http-runtime/src/herdr_queue_wake.rs and herdr_queue_wake_escalation.rs, so retained-log and doctor projection filtering cannot select it. Remediation: add subsystem = \"received_hook_selector\" and action = \"herdr_prompt\" (match the naming the sibling sites use; verify and use their actual field values). Verify the line and the sibling claim with grep before writing; correct if they differ and say so. Sweep: list every warn!/error! macro in those three files that lacks a subsystem field; if there are more, add one Occurrence per extra site (INTEGRATE-2, INTEGRATE-3, ...) and set repeatable true; otherwise repeatable false." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ax" ;
  triage:triageMode "phase_end_review" ;
